|YK0SYNTAX
======
|YKBset <option> <value>|YK0

DESCRIPTION
===========
The set command allows you to customize several different features
as described below:
Option may be one of the following:
  |YKBmail <e-mail address>|YK0   
    Sets your current e-mail address.
  |YKBforwarding <on/off>|YK0
    Forward your mudmail to your e-mail?
  |YKBvismail <off|on>|YK0
    Allows your e-mail address to be seen by others.
  |YKBweb <valid URL>|YK0
    Adds your web page address to your 'finger' info.
  |YKBprompt <string>|YK0
    Sets the string used as your prompt.
    As a wiz, you can add the following vars:
        %d = current working directory
        %i = current invis level
        %wi = whoinvis indicator
        %f = fakeidle indicator
        %e = environment (D/P for dev/prod)
  |YKBmonitor <off|on|bar>|YK0
    Sets how your remaining HP/SP are shown.
  |YKBautoexits <off|on>|YK0
    Sets whether detailed exit information is shown.
  |YKBanonymous <off|on>|YK0
    Sets how anonymous you are to the other players.
  |YKBterm <ansi|vt100|vt52|none>|YK0
    Sets which terminal type you're using to connect.
  |YKBtimestamps <off|on>|YK0
    Sets timestamps on|off when viewing channel histories.
  |YKBbrief <off|on>|YK0
    Sets the amount of room descriptions that are shown.
  |YKBlanguage <race>|YK0
    Set your default language to speak with.
  |YKBcolorblock <off|on>|YK0
    Setting this |YKBon|YK0 locks the color of your channels
    to the value you set in 'color'. Leaving it |YKBoff|YK0
    allows you to see when players use color codes
    in their channel messages.
  |YKBshowmulties [off|main|on]|YK0
    Setting this to |YKBON|YK0 allows other players to see
    a list of your Main character and registered
    multies at the bottom of your finger info. This
    allows players to learn your other characters if
    you choose.
    Setting this to |YKBMAIN|YK0 allows other players to see
    only your |YKBMAIN|YK0 character at the bottom of your
    finger info, unless the 'finger' is targeting
    your main character already.
    Setting this to |YKBOFF|YK0 does not show your multies
    to other players.
    Default setting is |YKBOFF|YK0.

